WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.530
Film Courage: We had another question come
in [from the viewers].

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:03.199
It’s much more light-hearted than our previous
conversation.

00:00:03.199 --> 00:00:04.470
Bing Liu, filmmaker of MINDING THE GAP documentary:
What’s their name?

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.129
Film Courage: His name is Nafis Mustafa.

00:00:06.129 --> 00:00:08.920
Bing: Okay, I’m just hoping for another
ZombieDude64.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:13.580
Film Courage: Nafis, he has commented before
and he’s great.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.379
He writes “What would be your core advice
to aspiring filmmaker?”

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:20.440
So let’s supposed somebody is 14 again [like
Bing’s story] but not with mini-DV (in the

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:21.440
current form).

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:25.650
This time they have a 4k camera or another
amazing camera that they’re currently using.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.260
Bing: Do it for the love, you know?

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.450
When I was growing up in Rockford [Illinois,
where much of MINDING THE GAP is filmed] being

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:32.719
a filmmaker was just such a realistic thing.

00:00:32.719 --> 00:00:34.649
I was just doing it for the love, right?

00:00:34.649 --> 00:00:38.699
I was emulating things, it felt good to be
creative.

00:00:38.699 --> 00:00:45.120
But in terms of making a film, these things
take years.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.010
So don’t pick something that you’re not
truly passionate about.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:55.030
Pick something that you care about more than
just making a film.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:59.559
And I think everyone because of their personal
experience, because of where they come from,

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:03.219
because of the way they think, everyone has
at least one story within themselves that

00:01:03.219 --> 00:01:06.140
only they can tell and nobody else can tell.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:10.899
I think people should honor and respect that
for themselves and I don’t just mean making

00:01:10.899 --> 00:01:16.020
a personal film about themselves.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:23.590
We really need to sort of have understanding
across many different aisles and lines that

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:27.580
seem a little bit more highlighted these days,
lines of division.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.789
Film Courage: Absolutely.

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:32.830
What did you used to film the movie [MINDING
THE GAP on Hulu] with from the mini-DV camera

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:37.759
to there were other shots that definitely
were not mini-DV?

00:01:37.759 --> 00:01:41.359
Bing: I consider all that stuff archival.

00:01:41.359 --> 00:01:46.670
But so filming it with three different DSLRs
and c300.

